    <!-- TEAM -->
    <section id="team" class="py-12 bg-white">
      <div class="max-w-6xl mx-auto px-5 lg:px-8">
        <div class="mb-8">
          <span class="inline-block text-xs font-medium text-primary bg-primary/10 px-4 py-1.5 rounded-full mb-4">Our Team</span>
          <h2 class="font-serif text-2xl text-ink mb-2">Meet your psychologists</h2>
          <p class="text-ink-muted text-sm">Sessions are held in Turkish and English, in person or online.</p>
        </div>

        <div class="grid gap-6 lg:grid-cols-2">
          <article id="gokce-ince" class="bg-warm border border-warm-tertiary rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-5">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-primary/15 to-sage/20 flex items-center justify-center text-3xl">{% icon "person", "w-7 h-7" %}</div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink leading-tight">Gökçe İnce</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-primary mb-3">Clinical Psychologist</p>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Psychodynamic psychotherapy</span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Emerging adulthood</span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Adults</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
              <p>Completed an undergraduate degree in the Department of Psychology at Eastern Mediterranean University and a master's degree in the Clinical Psychology programme at Maltepe University. Clinical supervision is complete, and professional development continues through training and supervision in scientifically grounded psychotherapy approaches.</p>
              <p>Has gained experience with different age groups and in different working environments. Worked for many years as a psychologist at the Eastern Mediterranean University Psychological Counselling, Guidance and Research Centre (EMU-PDRAM), and also provided therapy at Yaşam Hospital.</p>
              <p>Works mainly with <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">emerging adulthood and with adults</strong>. In the therapy process, the aim is to accompany individuals as they come to understand the emotional, relational and psychological difficulties they meet in their lives, and as they explore more closely the bond they have with themselves, with their relationships and with their lives.</p>
              <p>Draws primarily on the psychodynamic psychotherapy approach. The psychodynamic approach focuses on understanding a person's present emotional and relational difficulties together with their past experiences, inner world and the relational patterns formed over time. Alongside this, other psychotherapy approaches are drawn on as well, taking into account each individual's needs, life story and circumstances; the therapy process is structured around the person, allowing for eclectic work. Importance is placed on bringing scientific knowledge and clinical experience together within a safe, ethical and collaborative therapeutic relationship.</p>
              <p>Works in Turkish and English, in person and online.</p>
            </div>
          </article>

          <article id="yaprak-parlan-yesilovali" class="bg-warm border border-warm-tertiary rounded-2xl p-6 lg:p-8">
            <div class="flex items-start gap-4 mb-5">
              <div class="w-16 h-16 shrink-0 rounded-full bg-gradient-to-br from-accent/10 to-warm-tertiary flex items-center justify-center text-3xl">{% icon "person", "w-7 h-7" %}</div>
              <div>
                <h3 class="font-serif text-xl text-ink leading-tight">Yaprak Parlan Yeşilovalı, MSc</h3>
                <p class="text-sm text-primary mb-3">Developmental Psychologist &amp; Psychotherapist</p>
                <div class="flex flex-wrap gap-2">
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Cognitive behavioural therapy</span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Children</span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Adolescents</span>
                  <span class="text-[11px] font-medium text-ink-muted bg-white border border-warm-tertiary px-2.5 py-1 rounded-full">Adults</span>
                </div>
              </div>
            </div>
            <div class="space-y-3 text-sm text-ink-muted leading-relaxed">
              <p>In therapy, the difficulty a person is living with is not taken as a single symptom or problem; it is considered as a whole, within their developmental period, life story, relationships and social environment. The work looks not only at today's problem, but also at where the person has come from, what has been happening in their life and where they would like to move towards.</p>
              <p>Cognitive Behavioural Therapy (CBT) is the main approach drawn on. CBT is used so that a person can understand their difficulties better, look with fresh eyes at the relationship they have with themselves and with what they have lived through, and develop new ways of coping that work in everyday life. Other psychotherapy approaches are also drawn on according to the individual's needs and goals. Works with <strong class="font-semibold text-ink">children, adolescents and adults</strong>.</p>
              <p>Undergraduate studies were completed at the University of Brighton in Applied Psychology and Criminology and in the EMU Department of Psychology, and a master's degree in Developmental Psychology at EMU. CBT training for children and adolescents was completed within a programme accredited by the Turkish Association for Cognitive and Behavioural Psychotherapies, and CBT training for adults at the Beck Institute. Professional development continues through current training and supervision.</p>
              <p>Worked as a lecturer in the EMU Department of Psychology and as a psychologist at the EMU Psychological Counselling, Guidance and Research Centre (EMU-PDRAM). Psychoeducation and counselling programmes for children, young people, women and adults were also prepared and run at various civil society organisations, alongside different projects with educators. Academic and applied experience at the university has formed a strong basis for the work carried out with young adults in particular.</p>
              <p>Psychotherapy is approached as a safe and collaborative process in which a person can express themselves as they are and look at what they have lived through from different angles. In therapy, the individual's needs, their own pace and their personal life experience are what matter.</p>
              <p>Works in Turkish and English, both in person and online.</p>
            </div>
          </article>
        </div>
      </div>
    </section>

